Running guide:

python galaxy_cli.py scan /path/to/images
python galaxy_cli.py preprocess --size 128
python galaxy_cli.py distances --n 500 --algo zlib
python galaxy_cli.py rms --k-min 2 --k-max 12
python galaxy_cli.py cluster --k 5
python galaxy_cli.py neighbors --query 3 --k 10
python galaxy_cli.py pipeline /data/galaxies --n 1000 --k 6


If you want to run whole dataset use this command:

# 1. Scan
python galaxy_cli.py scan /path/to/your/galaxy/images

# 2. Compute distances for ALL images (no --n limit = uses all scanned)
python galaxy_cli.py distances --algo zlib

# 3. Find optimal k (elbow diagram saved as PNG)
python galaxy_cli.py rms --k-min 2 --k-max 12 --runs 3

# 4. Cluster with your chosen k
python galaxy_cli.py cluster --k 6

# 5. Nearest neighbors for any image
python galaxy_cli.py neighbors --query 0 --k 10
